      "id": 1,
      "text": "Dahlgren’s naval base was named after Rear Admiral John A. Dahlgren, a pioneer of naval ordnance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dahlgren%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Naval Surface Warfare Center Dahlgren Division, a major weapons research facility, sits just east of town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dahlgren%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Dahlgren Heritage Museum opened in 2013, showcasing naval artifacts and local history for visitors and residents alike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dahlgrenmuseum.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Upper Machodoc Creek, an arm of the Potomac River, borders Dahlgren to the south and offers tidal marina access.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dahlgren%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dahlgren is part of the Northern Neck National Heritage Area, a region celebrated for its maritime and colonial legacy.",
